{"title":"1989 USAMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems from the <b>1989 <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"USAMO\">USAMO</a>.</b>\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For each positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, let\n</p>\n<div style=\"text-align:center;\">\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/5/5f5149c7302a43fa748443ad7a192ced2ed8aee3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n = 1 + \\frac 12 + \\frac 13 + \\cdots + \\frac 1n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"203\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/6/a760d48cfa5beee3ce0e9f49a78cc98bd5c1598a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_n = S_1 + S_2 + S_3 + \\cdots + S_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"232\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/8/0f8bfd1b54e0e29c765b7a794d0c1e14d266da9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U_n = \\frac{T_1}{2} + \\frac{T_2}{3} + \\frac{T_3}{4} + \\cdots + \\frac{T_n}{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"266\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p>\n</div>\n<p>Find, with proof, integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/9/8996c96b5bf370e21a81278b54c6203ee3a1be0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; a,\\ b,\\ c,\\ d &lt; 1000000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"195\" height=\"16\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/8/228208e58ea267d5895c1cd7918fe843ba31dbe0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{1988} = a S_{1989} - b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"140\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/c/55c002ecdd604508bef322f223fffd5db3d89d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U_{1988} = c S_{1989} - d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"142\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The 20 members of a local tennis club have scheduled exactly 14 two-person games among themselves, with each member playing in at least one game. Prove that within this schedule there must be a set of 6 games with 12 distinct players.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a98921ac8588f67c4d2279bba0fddeecb3107fe3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(z)= z^n + c_1 z^{n-1} + c_2 z^{n-2} + \\cdots + c_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"310\" height=\"21\" /> be a polynomial in the complex variable <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, with real coefficients <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/d/3bd87559f4e4c9af40246a0fdbafe6feab507414.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/8/4782f9100cc011f1d97a4dfc0517ad836176e58d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|P(i)| &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />. Prove that there exist real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/6/f36c82a9b9fe5c485dbd9230b0440c5578749ed7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(a + bi) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/7/d073646141e953c1b3d4049346c2a792e53c2c8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^2 + b^2 + 1)^2 &lt; 4 b^2 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"186\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be an acute-angled triangle whose side lengths satisfy the inequalities <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/5/a252cc19c08fe62efc73a6ae674fc651405ca92f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB &lt; AC &lt; BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"136\" height=\"15\" />. If point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the center of the inscribed circle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the center of the circumscribed circle, prove that line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/f/33f85e8c5408e12d1e17e232001b1d0613ab674a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IO$\" width=\"23\" height=\"12\" /> intersects segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be real numbers such that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/0/880de460dfd5f209804e09cfe5ea54292c9bbbd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(u + u^2 + u^3 + \\cdots + u^8) + 10u^9 = (v + v^2 + v^3 + \\cdots + v^{10}) + 10v^{11} = 8.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"562\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Determine, with proof, which of the two numbers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, is larger.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO\" title=\"1989 USAMO\">1989 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1989\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO\" title=\"1988 USAMO\">1988 USAMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_USAMO\" title=\"1990 USAMO\">1990 USAMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017200704\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.031 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.052 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 193/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1209/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 60/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5234/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   17.350      1 -total\n 57.90%   10.046      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n 40.81%    7.081      1 Template:USAMO_box\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4872:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017200704 and revision id 79443. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}